# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Fit (F, the API's `fit`) takes building systems into account: a document
# of one standalone ceiling moved away from the origin fits on it (issue
# 38 kept the camera where it was), and an upright system fits on its face.
# Camera fit needs the rendering/UI imports; run with an app validation bundle.
import ui/shell/bim_app_parts.dl

function check fit systems {boolean:condition} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function fit systems {a 64 bit floating-point number:value} is near {a 64 bit floating-point number:wanted}:
    execute:
        return (the absolute value of (value - wanted)) < 1e-6

set editor to a new bim editor
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set levelValue to the item at (the bim level index of editor's levelId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's levels's values)
set layout to @intrinsic("construct", a bim screen layout record, 1200.0, 800.0, 0.0, 600.0, 100.0, 750.0)
set camera to @intrinsic("construct", a bim camera record, (a cad vector2 with x 100.0 and y 100.0), 1.0, 0.5, 0.5, (a cad vector3 with x 100.0, y 100.0 and z 100.0), 1.0)

# A 4.8 x 3.6 m ceiling lying level at 2.5 m, moved to (10, 5): its face
# spans x 10 to 14.8 and y 5 to 8.6, so the camera targets (12.4, 6.8).
set ceilingId to add bim curtain wall on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 5.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 14.8 and y 5.0) rising 3.6 in bays of 1.2 by 1.2 of (the string form of "gypsum") to target
set bim setting (bim system level setting) of ceilingId to (2500 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
set fitted to the bim camera fitting editor in layout keeping camera
check fit systems ((fit systems fitted's target's x is near 12.4) and (fit systems fitted's target's y is near 6.8)) named (the string form of "a ceiling-only document fits on the ceiling")
check fit systems (fit systems fitted's target's z is near (levelValue's elevation + 2.5)) named (the string form of "the ceiling's height is its storey's elevation plus its level")
check fit systems ((fit systems fitted's centre's x is near 12.4) and (fit systems fitted's centre's y is near 6.8)) named (the string form of "the plan centres on the ceiling too")

# Turned 90 degrees about (10, 5) the ceiling lies across x 6.4 to 10.
set turnedId to add bim curtain wall on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 5.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 9.8) rising 3.6 in bays of 1.2 by 1.2 of (the string form of "gypsum") to target
set bim setting (bim system level setting) of turnedId to (2500 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
ignore (delete bim curtain wall ceilingId from target)
set turnedFit to the bim camera fitting editor in layout keeping camera
check fit systems ((fit systems turnedFit's target's x is near 8.2) and (fit systems turnedFit's target's y is near 7.4)) named (the string form of "a turned ceiling fits on where it lies")

# An upright system of 4 by 3 m from the origin: the box 0..4, 0, 0..3.
ignore (delete bim curtain wall turnedId from target)
ignore (add bim curtain wall on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 0.0) rising 3.0 in bays of 1.2 by 1.5 of (the string form of "aluminium") to target)
set uprightFit to the bim camera fitting editor in layout keeping camera
check fit systems (((fit systems uprightFit's target's x is near 2.0) and (fit systems uprightFit's target's y is near 0.0)) and (fit systems uprightFit's target's z is near (levelValue's elevation + 1.5))) named (the string form of "an upright system fits on its face")
